1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,667
The warning came too late.

2
00:00:01,897 --> 00:00:03,228
The ship had already sailed.

3
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:08,052
On January 21, 1895, the steamer Chicora

4
00:00:08,062 --> 00:00:10,552
left Milwaukee before dawn, bound for her

5
00:00:10,562 --> 00:00:12,530
home port, Saint Joseph, Michigan.

6
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:14,981
Her owner sent a warning not to sail.

7
00:00:15,211 --> 00:00:16,286
She was already gone.

8
00:00:16,936 --> 00:00:19,211
That day, a gale and a blizzard tore

9
00:00:19,221 --> 00:00:19,809
across the lake.

10
00:00:20,359 --> 00:00:22,037
The Chicora never made port.

11
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:24,651
Everyone aboard, about two dozen people,

12
00:00:24,661 --> 00:00:25,140
was lost.

13
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:28,213
Wreckage washed up between South Haven and

14
00:00:28,223 --> 00:00:28,854
